    "body": "## What does this implement/fix?\n\n| Property | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Method | `<init>` |\n| Class | `org.nick.wwwjdic.ocr.OcrFormEntity` |\n| File | `wwwjdic/src/org/nick/wwwjdic/ocr/OcrFormEntity.java` |\n| Specification | `Closeable_MeaninglessClose` |\n| Analysis tool | `humanoid` |\n\n## Summary\n\n### Observed dynamic-analysis failure\n\nThe dynamic-analysis run by `humanoid` reported (`Closeable_MeaninglessClose`) while exercising `org.nick.wwwjdic.ocr.OcrFormEntity.<init>`:\n\n> Closeable_MeaninglessClose close() has no effect.\n\n### Root cause\n\nThe reviewed constructor explicitly invokes `baos.close()` on a locally allocated `java.io.ByteArrayOutputStream`, a governed receiver for the reported Closeable_MeaninglessClose close event. The stream is subsequently retained in `buff` for later output (CLM-001, CLM-002, CLM-003, CLM-004).\n\n### Correction strategy\n\nApply the localized source-level conformance repair while leaving buffer construction, compression, retention, and entity serialization unchanged. Hold publication for review of deployed-platform behavior and any external lifecycle contract that pipeline validation cannot establish.\n\n### Coordinated changes\n\n- `wwwjdic/src/org/nick/wwwjdic/ocr/OcrFormEntity.java`: ByteArrayOutputStream.close() has no effect here and is removed without changing allocation, compression, stream ownership, serialized multipart content, or the existing constructor API.\n- `wwwjdic-android/src/test/java/org/nick/wwwjdic/ocr/OcrFormEntityClosePredicateTest.java`: Creates the requested deterministic source-level regression test. It verifies ByteArrayOutputStream allocation, bitmap compression into that stream, retention in buff, the buff.writeTo(os) serialization path, and absence of a close() invocation on the allocated stream.\n\n### Verification included\n\n- Run the patched module's Gradle build and compare any production failure with the previously documented failure reproduced on the unmodified base commit.\n- Run the patched module's unit-test task, including OcrFormEntityClosePredicateTest.\n- Compile the patched module's androidTest sources.\n- Execute OcrFormEntityClosePredicateTest to confirm the close predicate is absent and the compression and serialization path remains present.\n- Execute OcrFormEntityClosePredicateTest to confirm the ByteArrayOutputStream close predicate is absent and the allocation, compression, buff assignment, and buff.writeTo(os) predicates remain present.\n\n## How was this tested?\n\n- [x] Automated test coverage added in 1 test file(s)\n- [x] The patched module compiles successfully (`:wwwjdic:compileDebugSources`); the full multi-module build was not completed in this environment\n- [ ] Confirmed by a project maintainer\n\n## Additional context\n\nI’m an undergraduate Computer Engineering student at the University of Brasília (UnB), and this contribution is part of a research project involving static analysis of Android apps.\n\nI’m happy to adjust the implementation to better match the project’s architecture, coding conventions, or maintainers’ recommendations.",
